# regexes = regular expressions
# valdiates fields 
# used with emails for example
# . = any character except a new line
# * = 0 or more repitions
# + = 1 or more repitions
# {m} = m repitions ex: 3 repitions where m = 3
# {m,n} = m-n repitions ex:1-5 repitions where m = 1 and n = 5
# ^ = matches start of the string
# $ = matches end of the string just before the new line at the end of the string
# [] = set of characters
# [^] = completing the set
# \w = word character and undersocore and numbers
# /W = not a word character
# | = either a or b